{
    "word": "soupçon",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "fb2c7f49-2807-32ce-b2d9-4136b4dcc6aa",
                "word": "soupçon",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "95257b8e-6fa9-4ee7-b9c6-5a0d85a77751",
                        "entry_id": "fb2c7f49-2807-32ce-b2d9-4136b4dcc6aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "soupçons"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                        "entry_id": "fb2c7f49-2807-32ce-b2d9-4136b4dcc6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A very small amount; a hint; a trace, slight idea; an inkling."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bf4946fe-b8bd-40d7-8c62-bb57cee16c86",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "Add a soupçon of red pepper."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bbdb759-cd96-4676-b2e0-ffd131529b02",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "coffee with a soupçon of cognac"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ca6e07c4-e5fb-4889-9bd4-d5927950fc18",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "No one is so depraved that a soupçon of goodness cannot be found in them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6d4312b4-0a6e-4427-8600-ee9c4e67df67",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "Henrietta, her niece, looked much prettier than she really was; she had good dark eyes, to which a soupçon of rouge, put on with such skill that few suspected it, gave all possible brightness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9764433b-d195-4cda-afab-402d85545f27",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "Eleanor returned the pressure of the other's hand with an infinitesimal soupçon of a squeeze."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4048da66-9f7d-449a-86d6-39318647fe55",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "[…] and as he spoke, there was just a soupçon of foreign accent in the pronunciation of the French vowels, a certain drawl of o's and a's, that would have betrayed the Britisher to an observant ear."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a21ad70a-6424-4d85-ba14-e2c726e8a18e",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "Anthony was playing with an ancient tennis-ball, and he bounced it carefully on the floor several times before he answered with a soupçon of acidity:\n“You're a little idiot, Geraldine.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa4a6615-a340-44bd-bfbf-33c501988595",
                                "sense_id": "a21d74ca-d20e-310e-abda-9eff5eebb9bd",
                                "text": "There were times, during the first two years of the Biden presidency, when I came close to forgetting about it all: the taunts and the provocations; the incitements and the resentments; the disorchestrated reasoning; the verbal incontinence; the press conferences fueled by megalomania, vengeance, and a soupçon of hydroxychloroquine."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a0c80e2c-0991-3380-bd17-27158e96728a",
                        "entry_id": "fb2c7f49-2807-32ce-b2d9-4136b4dcc6aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A suspicion; a suggestion."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    }
